values
  ($t$0407$t$, $t$Brooklawn Borough$t$, $t$CAMDEN$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Brooklawn Borough fire official (Fire Department is the local enforcing agency) (town fire bureau)","Contact: 856-456-0750","How to apply: No smoke/CO certificate form or fee schedule was found on the Borough website. Contact the Borough office at 856-456-0750.","Fire official in the NJ state directory, updated 3/19/2026: Timothy O'Donnell · (856) 456-0750","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[]$j$::jsonb, null, $t$https://brooklawn-nj.com/departments/public-safety/fire/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$F Brooklawn Borough$t$, $t$638f01db634db06bd2a01a6ec0a347670240b360d5c06e484af667f54f5f7f24$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":2,"fee_ok":0,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":2,"quotes":3,"q_ok":2,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":1},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0407.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0407.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0416$t$, $t$Haddon Township$t$, $t$CAMDEN$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Haddon Township Construction & Zoning Office / Code Official (smoke and CO check done as part of the township Resale COC inspection) (town fire bureau)","Contact: 856-833-6265 · rsheppard@haddontwp.com","Apply: At least 14 business days before closing","How to apply: No separate smoke certificate application or fee was found. The Residential Resale / Tenant Change Inspection Application covers the smoke/CO (CSDCMAC) check together with the COC; see the the town certificate fees ($150 and up).","Fire official in the NJ state directory (town), updated 5/19/2026: William A Behnke · (856) 854-1176 · wbehnke@haddontwp.com","Smoke alarms no more than 10 years old; 10-year sealed battery units where battery units are allowed; hardwired alarms cannot be replaced with battery alarms","CO alarms less than 10 years old, in the hallway within 10 feet of all bedrooms","Homes with a low-voltage fire alarm system must have it tested by a certified alarm contractor before the inspection and show the certificate","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.haddontwp.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/Resale-Tenant-Change-Inspection-Form.pdf$t$, $t$https://www.haddontwp.com/departmets/construction-office/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.haddontwp.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/Resale-Tenant-Change-Inspection-Form.pdf","label":"Official source (haddontwp.com)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$I understand that any change of ownership/occupancy including storage of personal property may not occur, prior to successful inspection & possession of a (CSDCMAC) inspection.$t$, $t$c6eb4b654c1709e2cf48f384e4bafe6c8daa12d9cc66ea9c779f92bb699857ea$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":10,"fee_ok":0,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":10,"quotes":6,"q_ok":2,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":4},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0416.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0416.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0434$t$, $t$Voorhees Township$t$, $t$CAMDEN$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Voorhees Township Planning & Zoning Department (residential smoke/CO inspections, done with the resale certificate inspection) (town fire bureau)","Contact: 856-429-0647 · resales@voorheesnj.com","Apply: Same as the resale certificate; see resale fee tiers","How to apply: Use the Residential Resale Application from the Zoning Department; the smoke and CO alarm check is part of that inspection.","Fire official in the NJ state directory, updated 5/26/2026: Thomas O'Brien · (856) 783-6630 · tom.Obrien@vtfd66.org","Battery-only smoke alarms must be 10-year sealed units (per Voorhees resale packet and Fire Department page)","Carbon monoxide alarm within 10 feet of each sleeping area","Hardwired or monitored alarm systems cannot be downgraded to battery-only alarms","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://voorheesnj.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Residential-Resale-Application-7.02.2026.pdf$t$, $t$https://www.vtfd66.org/fire-prevention/inspection-bureau/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.vtfd66.org/fire-prevention/inspection-bureau/","label":"Official source (vtfd66.org)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$SMOKE DETECTOR INSPECTIONS FOR RESIDENTIAL PROPERTIES ARE COMPLETED THROUGH THE VOORHEES TOWNSHIP ZONING DEPARTMENT.$t$, $t$a757a8511cf9d1c7a4b7d183b2d3fcff69e71fc9ceb499ef448f116ea3000f34$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":6,"fee_ok":6,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":7,"q_ok":6,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":1},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0434.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0434.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0815$t$, $t$Pitman Borough$t$, $t$GLOUCESTER$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Borough of Pitman Fire Safety Official (Pitman Fire Department is the municipal local enforcing agency; inspections run through the Construction Office) (town fire bureau)","Contact: 856-589-2433 · firesafety@pitman.org","How to apply: Use the same Municipal Compliance for Housing and Fire Safety Inspection Application as the resale inspection. No separate smoke/CO certificate form or fee was found on the Borough site. Fire inspections are 'Call for availability' per the Construction page.","Fire official in the NJ state directory, updated 6/16/2026: Ryan Pierson · (856) 589-2433 · rpierson@eveshamfire.org","Smoke and CO detectors are checked on the combined Housing and Fire Safety inspection (Pitman checklist items 1 and 2)","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Combined Housing and Fire Safety Inspection, initial inspection per unit (one application and one payment block cover both)","amount":"$75.00"},{"label":"Combined Housing and Fire Safety Inspection, reinspection","amount":"$45.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.pitman.org/Construction/HOUSING-FIRE%20SAFETY%20INSPECTION%20APPLICATION.pdf$t$, $t$https://www.pitman.org/departments/construction___zoning/index.php$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.pitman.org/Construction/HOUSING-FIRE%20SAFETY%20INSPECTION%20APPLICATION.pdf","label":"Official source (pitman.org)"},{"url":"https://www.law.cornell.edu/regulations/new-jersey/N-J-A-C-5-70-2-3","label":"Official source (law.cornell.edu)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$F Pitman Borough$t$, $t$7a95f743efd62413987bd024f385c6babd970edb059aae3f422f26915adc0a20$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":4,"fee_ok":4,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":7,"q_ok":6,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":1},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0815.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0815.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0821$t$, $t$Westville Borough$t$, $t$GLOUCESTER$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Westville Fire District #1 (Office of the Fire Marshal) (fire district)","Contact: 856-456-9432","How to apply: No smoke certificate form or fee was found online. Call the Westville Fire District office at (856) 456-9432; the district lists a Housing Inspections contact at that number. The Borough's Certificate of Inspection also checks smoke alarms, CO alarms and the extinguisher.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (fire district), updated 9/15/2025: Timothy J. O'Donnell · (856) 456-9432","Smoke alarms (hardwired or 10-year sealed) must be less than 10 years old; locations that are hardwired must keep hardwired alarms","Smoke alarm on each level including the basement, within 10 feet outside bedrooms, and in every room used for sleeping","CO alarms (hardwired or battery) less than 10 years old, within 10 feet of each room used for sleeping","Fire extinguisher rated 2A:10B:C for residential use, within 10 feet of the kitchen on the way out, mounted no higher than 5 feet with its original hardware, not blocked","Low-voltage (monitored) smoke alarm systems need a letter from the alarm company showing a test in the last 30 days","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[]$j$::jsonb, null, $t$https://westvillefd.com/fire-district-contacts/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://westvillefd.com/fire-district-contacts/","label":"Official source (westvillefd.com)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$D Westville Borough$t$, $t$caa2b0525ea74fb92a6830fcefb2d27aeebe215d83c556724521e65000de1875$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":5,"fee_ok":5,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":5,"q_ok":4,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":1},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0821.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0821.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0902$t$, $t$East Newark Borough$t$, $t$HUDSON$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: East Newark Fire Prevention Bureau (town fire bureau)","Contact: Juan C. Barroso Jr., Fire Code Official · 973-481-2902, ext. 234 · fireprevention@boroughofeastnewark.com","How to apply: The smoke and carbon monoxide check is done as part of the resale Certificate of Occupancy process; the Borough's CO application has a Fire Department (smoke detectors) sign-off line. The Borough also posts an Application for One and Two Families, Certification of Smoke Detector and Carbon Monoxide Detector Compliance, from the Construction Code Department. Call the Fire Prevention Bureau to confirm how to schedule and pay.","Fire official in the NJ state directory, updated 7/13/2026: Juan C Barroso Jr · (973) 481-2902","Ten-year sealed battery smoke alarms (required since January 22, 2019) on each level and outside each sleeping area within 10 feet of bedrooms, on or near the ceiling","Carbon monoxide alarm (battery, hard-wired or plug-in) outside each sleeping area within 10 feet of bedrooms, UL 2034 listed","Borough handout (2020) still lists a 2A:10B:C portable fire extinguisher, no more than 10 pounds, mounted within 10 feet of each kitchen in the exit path; a kitchen-only extinguisher does not pass","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.boroughofeastnewark.com/_Content/pdf/forms/Smoke-Carbon-Monoxide-Certification.pdf$t$, $t$https://www.boroughofeastnewark.com/Departments/fire-prevention-bureau$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.boroughofeastnewark.com/Departments/fire-prevention-bureau","label":"Official source (boroughofeastnewark.com)"},{"url":"https://www.boroughofeastnewark.com/api/data/GetDirectoryDepartmentsData","label":"Official source (boroughofeastnewark.com)"},{"url":"https://www.boroughofeastnewark.com/_Content/pdf/minutes/2026-01-07-Council-Minutes.pdf","label":"Official source (boroughofeastnewark.com)"},{"url":"https://www.boroughofeastnewark.com/_Content/pdf/forms/Smoke-CO-Fire-Ext.pdf","label":"Official source (boroughofeastnewark.com)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Fire Code Official Juan C. Barroso Jr.$t$, $t$7d3b1519ce26add1c5c00fa218099b500601267090accbf9f1bb3f8201b8e06a$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":3,"fee_ok":3,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":13,"q_ok":13,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0902.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0902.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1104$t$, $t$Hightstown Borough$t$, $t$MERCER$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Hightstown Borough Code Enforcement / Construction Office (smoke detector compliance for the Borough fire code agency) (town fire bureau)","Contact: Dave Bell, Housing Inspector · (609) 490-5100 Ext 407 · DBell@HightstownBorough.com","How to apply: No separate smoke and carbon monoxide certificate form is posted. The smoke detector, CO detector and fire extinguisher items are on the inspection checklist of the Certificate of Compliance for Sale/Title Transfer application, so they appear to be checked in that inspection. Confirm with the Code Enforcement Office or the Fire Official whether a separate certificate or fee applies.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (town), updated 6/10/2022: Chad Reed · (609) 490-5100","Smoke detectors on each level and outside each sleeping area, 10 year sealed battery or hardwired","Carbon monoxide detector near all sleeping areas, less than 10 years old","The Borough sale form still lists an ABC fire extinguisher within 10 feet of the kitchen (form footer Revised: 01/2025, after the February 2025 state change)","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.hightstownborough.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/2026-CC-for-Sale-Transfer-Application-Rev-3.26.pdf$t$, $t$https://www.hightstownborough.com/construction-zoning/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.hightstownborough.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/2026-CC-for-Sale-Transfer-Application-Rev-3.26.pdf","label":"Official source (hightstownborough.com)"},{"url":"https://www.hightstownborough.com/construction-zoning/","label":"Official source (hightstownborough.com)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Smoke detectors on each level and outside each sleeping area. (10-year sealed or hard-wired)$t$, $t$6bd3ea65166a1850525243d59b5e3248512b94bfea689e85825e74fcf2697ec6$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":4,"fee_ok":4,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":12,"q_ok":12,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1104.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1104.json$t$, true)
